+# ADK Design Document (Aegis)
+
+Overview
+- Purpose: provide a standardized SDK and toolchain to build, test, verify and operate agents in Aegis.
+- Scope: Planner/Executor/Enforcer APIs, trace recorder, evidence bundling, HIL/sim adapters, CI/PoA integration, and provenance hooks.
+
+Core Concepts
+- Action / Observation schema (ops/adk/sdk/schemas.py): versioned, backward-compatible dataclasses serialized to dicts and ndjson.
+- Recorder (ops/adk/sdk/recorder.py): emits typed events (action.submitted, started, finished, policy.violation) into a trace ndjson for evidence.
+- Evidence (ops/adk/sdk/evidence.py): bundles traces + artifacts, computes SHA256, optionally signs with cosign KMS.
+- Agent runtime (ops/adk/sdk/agent.py): Agent.run_goal orchestrates Planner -> Enforcer -> Executor loop while recording events.
+
+API Contracts
+- Planner.propose(goal, state) -> [Action]. Deterministic for a given goal+state when used in reproducible tests.
+- Executor.execute(action, state) -> {status, evidence, details}
+- Enforcer.check(action, state) -> (allow: bool, reason: str)
+- Recorder emits ndjson-compatible trace file; evidence bundler must include that trace and related artifacts.
+
+File Formats
+- Trace: ndjson, each line { ts, type, payload } where payload embeds versioned Action/Observation dicts.
+- Evidence bundle: tar.gz with directory /evidence containing files and manifest.json with SHA256 entries.
+
+Provenance & Security
+- Evidence bundles are cosign-signed with a KMS-backed key; Rekor server should be configured in CI to record the signature.
+- Builders producing agent artifacts must be hardened and demonstrated via ops/ci scripts.
+- ADK exposes an evidence.sign helper to call cosign; CI must store COSIGN_KMS_URI secret.
+
+HIL/Sim Integration
+- Executor implementations plug in HIL adapters (direct or rabbit/k8s jobs) to execute actions in HIL; sample SimExecutor is a smoke harness.
+- Recorder traces are identical across sim/HIL to ensure reproduciability.
+
+Formal & Certification Mapping
+- Map each HARA mitigation to:
+  - evidence trace(s): path to trace.ndjson
+  - HIL bundle(s): cosign-signed tar.gz
+  - formal runs: apalache outputs referencing agent model or invariants
+- Provide a safety_case template (docs/safety/safety_case_template.md) to attach ADK outputs.
+
+CI & Dev Flow
+- Local dev: run sample agent and inspect /tmp/adk_sample/
+- CI: run unit tests, sim integration, produce adk_evidence.tar.gz, sign with cosign KMS URI (secret).
+- PoA: include adk evidence via ops/adk/poa_integration.sh into the PoA auditor bundles.
+
+Extensibility
+- Provide language bindings (Python primary) and design for pluggable executors/enforcers/planners.
+- Keep schema versions to allow migrations and validators that check event compatibility.
+
