+# ADK Operator Runbook
+
+Quick start (local test)
+1. Install deps:
+   pip install -r ops/adk/requirements.txt
+2. Run unit tests:
+   pytest -q ops/adk/tests/test_recorder.py
+3. Run sample agent:
+   python3 ops/adk/sample_agent/sample_agent.py --goal '{"command":"status"}' --out /tmp/adk_sample
+4. Inspect /tmp/adk_sample/trace.ndjson and /tmp/adk_sample/adk_evidence.tar.gz
+
+CI prerequisites
+- Set COSIGN_KMS_URI in secrets for signing evidence bundles.
+- Optionally set S3_UPLOAD for evidence upload in CI.
+
+HIL integration
+- Replace SimExecutor with a HILExecutor that calls your bench orchestrator and returns evidence file paths.
+- Ensure the HIL executor produces the same action result format so traces are compatible.
+
+Provenance test
+1. On builder, run ops/ci/builder_harden_and_cosign_automate.sh to validate cosign signing.
+2. Run ADK CI integration step to see signed evidence produced in CI.
+
+Certification evidence
+- Use ops/adk/poa_integration.sh to attach ADK bundles to the PoA auditor bundle and include in your safety case.
